@*
    The document itself.

    Two things here are load-bearing rather than boilerplate:

    * alvo.js is loaded in <head>, not at the end of <body>. It applies the stored theme before the
      first paint — a theme applied after paint is a flash, and under server-interactive rendering
      the first paint happens before hydration, so there is a real window to flash in.

    * The stylesheet and the script are named through AlvoAdminAssets rather than spelled here, so
      a rename is a compiler error instead of a blank page.

    * The render mode is decided here, PER REQUEST, and each of the three obvious alternatives is
      wrong in its own way. Declaring it on each page leaves the LAYOUT static — the sidebar, the
      theme toggle and the ⌘K palette are rendered outside the page's subtree, so their handlers are
      never wired and the keyboard silently does nothing. Declaring it on the layout does not
      compile at runtime: a layout receives `Body` as a `RenderFragment`, and a delegate cannot
      cross a static-to-interactive boundary. Declaring it unconditionally on the router makes the
      SIGN-IN page interactive too, and an interactive page cannot reliably post an
      antiforgery-protected form — the token is rendered over a circuit while the cookie that
      validates it belongs to an earlier response, so the post is refused, silently, because a
      refused token redirects back to the same screen.

      So: interactive for every page except the ones that opt out with
      `[ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]`, which `AcceptsInteractiveRouting` reports. Today that is
      the sign-in screen, and it is the screen whose whole job is an ordinary form post.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="@AlvoAdminAssets.Mark" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@AlvoAdminAssets.StyleSheet" />
    <script src="@AlvoAdminAssets.Script"></script>
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="PageRenderMode" />
</head>
<body>
    <AdminRoutes @rendermode="PageRenderMode" />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

@code {
    /// <summary>The request being rendered, when one is rendering.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? Http { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Server-interactive for every page that has not opted out.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <see langword="null"/> means statically rendered. The check is the framework's own, so a
    /// page opts out by carrying <c>[ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]</c> rather than by being listed
    /// here — a list would be a second place to keep in step with the pages.
    /// </remarks>
    private IComponentRenderMode? PageRenderMode
        => Http?.AcceptsInteractiveRouting() is true ? RenderMode.InteractiveServer : null;
}
